Package: CDRscope
Type: Package
Title: Interpretable TCR/BCR Repertoire Analysis with Enhanced Features and
    Multi-Chain Support
Version: 2.4.0
Date: 2026-08-27
Authors@R: person("CDRscope", "Author", email = "cdrscope@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: CDRscope Author
Maintainer: CDRscope Author <cdrscope@example.com>
Description: An interpretable analysis framework for TCR/BCR immune repertoires.
    v2.0 adds multi-chain support (single/paired/all), RA-enhanced feature
    engineering (65 features across 11 modules), advanced classifiers (Random
    Forest, LASSO, XGBoost, Ensemble), and ESM-2 protein language model embedding
    with parametric UMAP. v2.1 adds a complete closed-loop analysis pipeline with
    10 modules: input, feature engineering, ESM-2 embedding, reference map
    projection, classification, UMAP visualization, domain-level significance
    analysis, breakthrough analysis (expansion gradient, UMAP axis decoding,
    disease scoring, sequence network), biological validation (frequency
    redistribution, citrullination-hydrophobicity axis, HLA stratification),
    and automated HTML report generation. The reference map provides a fixed
    UMAP space for cross-project comparison. Integrates six research directions
    into interpretable concept axes, builds a concept-bottleneck embedding
    space, separates diseases
    with explainable classifiers, and discovers biomarkers at both statistical
    and sequence levels. Designed in the style of Seurat: a single S4 object
    carrying clones, features, embeddings and markers through a piped workflow.
